1
00:01:53,800 --> 00:01:54,650
不
No!

2
00:02:03,200 --> 00:02:04,950
走
Hey! Go!

3
00:03:26,200 --> 00:03:28,370
那是谁
The hell was that?

4
00:03:28,450 --> 00:03:29,750
我不知道
I don't know.

5
00:03:29,830 --> 00:03:33,170
- 我们得帮帮他 - 不 你们快跑
- We have to get him help. -No. You need to run.

6
00:03:34,920 --> 00:03:37,590
我叫丹尼 我正在追杀手和会的人
My name is Danny. I'm hunting members of the Hand.

7
00:03:38,510 --> 00:03:40,220
我想你就是我们要找的人
I think you're the man we're looking for.

8
00:03:41,670 --> 00:03:42,680
铁拳
Iron Fist.

9
00:03:43,890 --> 00:03:45,180
回去吧
Go home.

10
00:03:48,770 --> 00:03:50,230
你知道我是谁
You know who I am?

11
00:03:53,100 --> 00:03:56,190
你的战斗 不在这里
The war you're fighting... it's not here.

12
00:03:59,070 --> 00:04:00,780
而在纽约
It's in New York City.

13
00:04:02,740 --> 00:04:05,120
别 嘿
No... No! Hey!

14
00:04:05,950 --> 00:04:06,950
嘿
Hey.

15
00:05:34,450 --> 00:05:35,830
关门了
Closing time.

16
00:05:37,330 --> 00:05:38,420
回家吧
Go home.

17
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:42,630
拜托 晚上才刚刚开始好吧
Come on, the night's just getting started.

18
00:05:42,710 --> 00:05:43,960
晚上
Night?

19
00:05:47,890 --> 00:05:50,010
该死
Ah, shit!

20
00:05:50,890 --> 00:05:52,970
不
No!

21
00:05:54,100 --> 00:05:56,140
先生 先生
Excuse me! Excuse me, sir!

22
00:05:56,230 --> 00:05:57,440
我很抱歉
No, um, I'm so sorry.

23
00:05:57,520 --> 00:05:59,100
- 这是我的车 - 不再是了
- This is my car. - Not anymore.

24
00:05:59,190 --> 00:06:01,730
今早9点开始这就是市政财产了 你停在了装卸专用区域
At nine a.M., it became city property. Loading zone only.

25
00:06:01,810 --> 00:06:03,650
- 求你了 我可以挪走 - 已经挂上拖车了
- Please. I can move it. - Not once it's hitched.

26
00:06:03,730 --> 00:06:05,500
但你可以在下午六点前
But you can come to the impound

27
00:06:05,500 --> 00:06:08,110
到49号大街的扣押区认领取回你的车
on 49th to reclaim it any time before six p.M.

28
00:06:09,110 --> 00:06:10,700
洛伊德 你在干什么
Lloyd, what the hell are you doing?

29
00:06:15,750 --> 00:06:16,750
什么
What?

30
00:06:17,870 --> 00:06:19,540
有问题吗
We got a problem?

31
00:06:19,620 --> 00:06:21,080
我昨天接到一个电话
I got a call yesterday.

32
00:06:21,170 --> 00:06:23,300
又一个制片人想拍你的故事
A second producer who wants to tell your story.

33
00:06:23,380 --> 00:06:24,380
没门
Hard pass.

34
00:06:24,460 --> 00:06:26,300
纽约喜欢赢家 不管你怎么想
New York loves a winner, and like it or not,

35
00:06:26,380 --> 00:06:29,180
你打败一个超级大反派
you stood up to a really awful person and won.

36
00:06:29,260 --> 00:06:31,390
你知道要达到你现在这种宣传热度 政论家们得开价多高吗
You know how much publicists charge for that kind of attention?

37
00:06:31,470 --> 00:06:32,510
要花多少钱才能让这个热度下去
How much to make it stop?

38
00:06:32,600 --> 00:06:34,510
我只是说 你可以考虑一下
I'm just saying, you might wanna consider it.

39
00:06:34,600 --> 00:06:37,430
在你再次工作前 这可以帮你糊口
It could help keep your bills paid until you start working again.

40
00:06:37,520 --> 00:06:39,270
- 我还饿不死 - 暂时而已
- My bills aren't a problem. - Not yet.

41
00:06:39,350 --> 00:06:41,520
你好歹有开始接业务电话吧
Have you at least started answering the phone?

42
00:06:43,820 --> 00:06:47,110
只有你才能把这种大好事看做坏事
Only you could turn that big personal victory into a defeat.

43
00:06:47,190 --> 00:06:49,990
- 你知道你问题在哪吗 -
- You know what your problem is? - Sentences that start like that.

44
00:06:50,070 --> 00:06:52,370
你还不能接受你现在的身份
You're not comfortable with what you've become.

45
00:06:52,450 --> 00:06:53,810
杰西卡 你现在是一个
Jessica, you are now a

46
00:06:53,810 --> 00:06:56,290
- 十足的超级英 - 别说那个词
- full-blown super-- -Do not say the H-word.

47
00:06:56,370 --> 00:06:59,160
杰西卡 我已经很头痛了
Jess, I-- -I've got enough of a headache as it is.

48
00:06:59,250 --> 00:07:01,330
我只是说 你可以回家 睡一觉
I'm just saying, you might wanna consider going home,

49
00:07:01,420 --> 00:07:03,960
然后重返现实社会
getting some sleep, rejoining society.

50
00:07:04,040 --> 00:07:05,420
我不是在和你说话嘛
I'm talking to you.

51
00:07:05,500 --> 00:07:07,010
我很感激这一点
And I appreciate that.

52
00:07:09,630 --> 00:07:11,840
- 这里面是有威士忌吗 - 哦对 这杯是我的
- Is there whiskey in this? -Oh, yeah, that's mine.

53
00:07:41,750 --> 00:07:44,000
看来你把上头各项关系都疏通好了
Looks like all of your paper-pushing worked.

54
00:07:45,670 --> 00:07:48,630
放这个超级明星走吧 让他离开这里
Uncuff the superstar. Get him out of my sight.

55
00:07:59,270 --> 00:08:00,270
我的错
My bad.

56
00:08:03,060 --> 00:08:04,060
这是你的
These belong to you.

57
00:08:21,120 --> 00:08:23,290
卢卡斯先生 还是凯奇先生
Mr. Lucas? Mr. Cage?

58
00:08:24,080 --> 00:08:26,710
- 你喜欢哪个 我忘了 - 凯奇
- Which do you prefer? I forget. - Cage.

59
00:08:28,380 --> 00:08:31,170
- 我认识你吗 - 富兰克林 尼尔森
- Do I know you? -Franklin Nelson.

60
00:08:31,260 --> 00:08:34,800
你的案子是我处理的 我们通过很多次电话
I ran point on your case. We spoke on the phone... A lot.

61
00:08:34,880 --> 00:08:36,390
你话很多
You spoke a lot.

62
00:08:36,470 --> 00:08:38,060
只有在工作的时候
As long as it worked.

63
00:08:38,850 --> 00:08:41,850
- 谢谢 - 谢你朋友鲍比 菲什吧
- I appreciate it. - Appreciate your friend Bobby Fish.

64
00:08:41,930 --> 00:08:44,140
我们可是翻阅了好多材料
We all did some impressive book-cracking.

65
00:08:44,230 --> 00:08:45,650
再说 你毫发无伤
Plus, you made it through a

66
00:08:45,650 --> 00:08:48,020
就逃出了监狱
prison stint without throwing a single punch.

67
00:08:48,110 --> 00:08:49,770
我相信这很难吧 对于像你这样
I'm sure that was hard for a person with your...

68
00:08:49,860 --> 00:08:51,730
- 我知道 - 名声的人
- I know. -...reputation.

69
00:08:52,320 --> 00:08:55,530
- 克莱尔来了吗 - 这里只有律师能进
- Is, uh... Claire coming? -It's lawyers only in here.

70
00:08:56,700 --> 00:08:59,280
请见谅 我还得去赶公交
Well, if you'll excuse me, I have a bus to catch.

71
00:08:59,370 --> 00:09:02,290
当然 噢 最后一件事
Of course. Uh, just one last thing.

72
00:09:03,330 --> 00:09:06,620
霍加斯 赵 本诺维茨律所为您服务
The law firm of Hogarth, Chao & Benowitz is at your disposal.

73
00:09:06,710 --> 00:09:09,130
如果你需要帮忙重新开始
In case you need help starting over.

74
00:09:09,210 --> 00:09:10,800
我不打算重新开始 尼尔森先生
I'm not starting over, Mr. Nelson.

75
00:09:11,960 --> 00:09:13,220
我会向前看的
I'm moving forward.

76
00:09:14,090 --> 00:09:15,680
人们叫我福基
People call me Foggy.

77
00:09:15,760 --> 00:09:16,760
你居然愿意让人这么叫你
And you let them?

78
00:09:24,100 --> 00:09:26,140
根据在案记录 你曾说50号和10号大街的新
You're on record as saying that the new subway station

79
00:09:26,230 --> 00:09:29,940
地铁站将会是 引用你的原话 有益公众的
at 50th and 10th would be, quote, "Good for the community."

80
00:09:30,020 --> 00:09:33,400
完全是引用原话 有益公众的
Would be quote-- quote, unquote, "Good for the community."

81
00:09:33,490 --> 00:09:36,490
伯克维兹先生 以你专业
Mr. Berkowitz, in your professional-- -

82
00:09:38,030 --> 00:09:40,580
你在干什么
What the hell are you doing?

83
00:09:40,660 --> 00:09:42,490
干嘛 我要打爆你的狗头
'Sup, man? I'll bust your goddamn head!

84
00:09:42,580 --> 00:09:44,660
- 是吗 我们走 - 发生了什么
- Oh, yeah? Let's go, then. - What's up?

85
00:09:44,750 --> 00:09:47,290
- 你想试试吗 - 快点 我们走
- You wanna try something? - Come at me. Let's go!

86
00:09:49,420 --> 00:09:51,920
纽约警察局 散开 够了
NYPD! Break it up! That's enough.

87
00:09:52,500 --> 00:09:54,880
- 你 到人行道上去 - 好的警官
- You, up on the sidewalk. - Yes, sir, officer.

88
00:09:58,640 --> 00:09:59,640
伯克维兹先生
Mr. Berkowitz...

89
00:09:59,720 --> 00:10:02,560
从你专业观点来看 这个地铁站对亚伦 詹姆斯有益了吗
In your professional opinion, was it good for Aaron James?

90
00:10:02,640 --> 00:10:03,960
我们深切同情这个家庭的不幸遭遇
Our sympathies go out to the family.

91
00:10:03,970 --> 00:10:05,480
整件事 非常不幸
The whole thing... It's very unfortunate.

92
00:10:05,560 --> 00:10:06,760
你那时候知道这些在你
Were you aware the products used

93
00:10:06,760 --> 00:10:08,520
新地铁站使用的产品对孩子有害吗
in your new station were hazardous to children?

94
00:10:08,600 --> 00:10:09,900
- 反对 - 我会换个说法
- Objection! -I'll rephrase.

95
00:10:09,980 --> 00:10:11,880
你使用的这种橡胶有哪些优点
What was attractive about Endexoprene?

96
00:10:11,880 --> 00:10:13,190
强韧 耐久
It's strong. It's durable.

97
00:10:13,280 --> 00:10:15,990
- 以及价格便宜一半 - 我是做生意的
- And half the price? - Well, I do run a business.

98
00:10:16,070 --> 00:10:18,570
为了节约钱就把人们置于危险之中 值得吗
Is it worth endangering people in the interest of saving money?

99
00:10:19,740 --> 00:10:21,160
所有材料都是测试过的
All materials are tested.

100
00:10:21,240 --> 00:10:22,780
在发现该产品有危害的报告公之于众以后
The moment those findings were made public,

101
00:10:22,870 --> 00:10:25,410
我们公司立刻更换了剩下所有地铁站内使用的橡胶粉砂浆
our company replaced that mortar in all remaining stations.

102
00:10:25,500 --> 00:10:27,330
公之于众
"Made public."

103
00:10:29,960 --> 00:10:31,130
这是什么意思
What do you mean?

104
00:10:32,460 --> 00:10:35,340
你是指那份9月29号公布的报告吗
Are you referring to a report released on September 29th?

105
00:10:35,420 --> 00:10:36,610
法官大人 他正在要求
Your Honor, he's asking my

106
00:10:36,610 --> 00:10:38,800
我的委托人回答不合理的具体细节
client to respond with unreasonable specificity.

107
00:10:38,880 --> 00:10:40,490
伯克维兹先生 如果我没有记错
Mr. Berkowitz, if memory serves me right,

108
00:10:40,490 --> 00:10:42,010
三个月之前 你的办公室曾在6月3号
your office received an urgent delivery

109
00:10:42,090 --> 00:10:44,930
收到过一份来自安全委员会的紧急文件
from the Safety Commission on June 3rd. Three months earlier.

110
00:10:45,010 --> 00:10:47,100
我很好奇 这是否与本案中有质量问题的橡胶有关呢
I'm curious, did that have anything to do with Endexoprene?

111
00:10:47,180 --> 00:10:48,230
我对此毫不知情
I don't know anything about that.

112
00:10:48,310 --> 00:10:49,480
法官大人 除非默多克先生
Your Honor, unless Mr. Murdock

113
00:10:49,560 --> 00:10:50,810
可以证明我的委托人确实
can prove my client actually

114
00:10:50,810 --> 00:10:52,810
收到了这些他口中所谓的文件 否则
received these hypothetical documents, then--

115
00:10:52,900 --> 00:10:54,310
这与他收没收到那份文件无关
It's not about whether he received them.

116
00:10:54,310 --> 00:10:55,690
而是在于他是否刻意忽略了它
It's whether he willfully ignored them.

117
00:10:55,780 --> 00:10:56,710
法官大人 我要求将这份紧急文件的
Your Honor, I ask that this

118
00:10:56,710 --> 00:10:58,280
发送记录作为证据呈上
record of delivery be admitted into evidence.

119
00:10:58,360 --> 00:11:01,410
- 我是说 我每天收到很多类似的文件 - 你觉得哪种情况更糟
- I mean, I get a lot of those. - What would you say is worse?

120
00:11:01,490 --> 00:11:03,370
为削减成本而忽视重要的相关数据
Ignoring data in the interest of cutting costs?

121
00:11:03,450 --> 00:11:05,660
还是出于过失而没有像法庭提供能够证明你
Or neglecting to supply the court with records that might prove

122
00:11:05,740 --> 00:11:07,160
你有意陷他人与危险之中的记录
you purposely put people in danger?

123
00:11:07,250 --> 00:11:08,500
- 包括 - 法官大人
- Including - Your Honor

124
00:11:08,580 --> 00:11:09,610
包括这位年轻人
Including this young man,

125
00:11:09,610 --> 00:11:11,250
亚伦 詹姆斯 他可能永远都没法走路了
Aaron James, who might never walk again.

126
00:11:11,330 --> 00:11:14,340
- 法官大人 我们申请休庭 - 不需要 我讲完了
- Your Honor, we would like a recess. - No need. I'm done.

127
00:11:15,250 --> 00:11:16,630
我觉得他也要玩完了
I think he is, too.

128
00:11:25,720 --> 00:11:28,430
一千一百万美金的赔偿款
$11 million!

129
00:11:29,140 --> 00:11:30,350
谢谢你 默多克先生
Thank you, Mr. Murdock.

130
00:11:30,440 --> 00:11:32,400
- 这是我的荣幸 - 谢谢
- Oh, my pleasure. -Thank you.

131
00:11:32,480 --> 00:11:33,940
我真为你感到高兴
I'm so happy for you.

132
00:11:38,190 --> 00:11:39,240
天哪
God.

133
00:11:42,110 --> 00:11:43,110
嗨
Hey.

134
00:11:44,530 --> 00:11:46,990
- 你还好吗 - 是的
- You okay? - Yeah.

135
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:54,170
介意我告诉你一些事情吗
Mind if I tell you something?

136
00:11:55,540 --> 00:11:56,750
讲吧
Sure.

137
00:11:59,420 --> 00:12:01,590
这笔钱对你父母很有帮助
That money is really gonna help your parents.

138
00:12:02,760 --> 00:12:04,600
但是对你来说 从现在起
But for you, from here on out...

139
00:12:04,600 --> 00:12:06,550
一切只会变得更难 亚伦
it's only gonna get harder, Aaron.

140
00:12:07,930 --> 00:12:10,480
你知道你艰难的人生马拉松才刚刚开始
You realize you're only at mile one of the marathon...

141
00:12:11,770 --> 00:12:12,770
对吧
right?

142
00:12:13,900 --> 00:12:15,860
所有人都会告诉你应该要怎么想
Everybody's gonna tell you how to feel.

143
00:12:16,860 --> 00:12:18,320
医生会叫你保持乐观
Doctors are gonna tell you to stay positive.

144
00:12:18,400 --> 00:12:20,280
你的家人会告诉你不要为自己感到悲哀
Your family's gonna tell you not to feel sorry for yourself.

145
00:12:20,360 --> 00:12:22,190
你的治疗师会告诉你不要生气
Your therapist is gonna tell you not to be angry--

146
00:12:22,280 --> 00:12:23,660
我已经很生气了
I'm already angry.

147
00:12:24,950 --> 00:12:26,280
对谁生气
At who?

148
00:12:28,790 --> 00:12:30,080
所有人
Everyone.

149
00:12:32,080 --> 00:12:33,920
我只想回到从前的生活
I just want my life back.

150
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:35,500
这是不可能的
They can't give you that.

151
00:12:38,670 --> 00:12:40,000
或许你能重新走路
Maybe you'll walk again.

152
00:12:40,840 --> 00:12:41,880
希望你可以做到
I hope so.

153
00:12:43,590 --> 00:12:45,010
但是也许你做不到
But maybe you won't.

154
00:12:46,010 --> 00:12:50,310
但在这个愈发艰难的过程中 学会面对这一切
But your ability to get through it... as this gets harder...

155
00:12:51,350 --> 00:12:52,600
比强颜欢笑
that is a hundred times more

156
00:12:52,600 --> 00:12:54,520
假装一切都好
powerful than slapping a smile on your face

157
00:12:54,600 --> 00:12:56,520
要重要一百倍
and pretending like everything's just fine.

158
00:12:57,770 --> 00:13:00,190
你能明白吗
Do you understand?

159
00:13:03,150 --> 00:13:04,700
嘿 听着
Hey, listen...

160
00:13:05,610 --> 00:13:07,620
没有人可以让你回到以前的生活 亚伦
no one can give you your life back, Aaron.

161
00:13:09,160 --> 00:13:11,870
你必须 你只能靠自己
You have... You gotta take it back.

162
00:13:18,920 --> 00:13:19,920
我们走吧
Let's go.

163
00:13:38,770 --> 00:13:40,570
恭喜你 默多克先生
Congratulations, Mr. Murdock.

164
00:13:41,610 --> 00:13:43,990
哦 谢谢你 佩奇小姐
Oh. Thank you, Ms. Page.

165
00:13:44,690 --> 00:13:47,010
没关系的 你可以为自己感到
It's okay. You can be proud of yourself.

166
00:13:47,010 --> 00:13:48,740
一点点骄傲 我不会告诉其他人的
A little. I won't tell anyone.

167
00:13:50,410 --> 00:13:51,830
你 是来采访我的吗
You, uh, here for a statement?

168
00:13:52,580 --> 00:13:53,660
是的
Uh, yeah.

169
00:13:55,370 --> 00:13:59,170
嘿 你想不想去 边吃边做采访
Hey, you maybe wanna go... do that over a bite or...

170
00:14:00,460 --> 00:14:02,670
哦 额 当然了
Oh, uh... Sure, yeah.

171
00:14:02,750 --> 00:14:05,800
- 额 可以给我5分钟吗 - 好的
- Um... can you give me five minutes? - Mm-hmm.

172
00:14:09,090 --> 00:14:11,850
- 默多克先生 - 默多克先生
- Mr. Murdock... - Mr. Murdock, sir...

173
00:14:11,930 --> 00:14:12,850
怎么了
Yes...

174
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:08,210
你抛弃了他们
You abandoned them.

175
00:16:09,710 --> 00:16:12,720
拜你所赐 手和会赢了
Because of you, the Hand has won.

176
00:16:13,970 --> 00:16:15,050
我很抱歉
I'm sorry.

177
00:16:15,140 --> 00:16:16,390
在他们把你培养起来之后
After they raised you...

178
00:16:17,140 --> 00:16:19,270
他们给了你一切 你
after they gave you everything you are...

179
00:16:20,060 --> 00:16:21,890
你却任他们死去
you let them die.

180
00:16:21,980 --> 00:16:23,520
不
No.

181
00:16:24,100 --> 00:16:25,270
不是的
No!

182
00:16:27,230 --> 00:16:29,230
- 丹尼 醒醒 - 不
- Danny. Wake up. -No!

183
00:16:29,320 --> 00:16:30,780
不
No!

184
00:16:30,860 --> 00:16:31,860
丹尼
Danny.

185
00:16:36,320 --> 00:16:37,410
你没事吧
You okay?

186
00:16:41,540 --> 00:16:42,710
没事
Yeah.

187
00:16:44,040 --> 00:16:45,880
只是 只是因为有点颠簸
It's just the... It's just the turbulence.

188
00:16:47,750 --> 00:16:49,880
我觉得我永远都没法习惯飞机的颠簸了
I don't think I'll ever get used to it.

189
00:16:58,600 --> 00:17:00,810
- 丹尼 - 我
- Danny... - I'm...

190
00:17:03,940 --> 00:17:05,350
我要去找机长
I'm gonna go check with the pilot.

191
00:17:07,650 --> 00:17:08,650
丹尼
Danny.

192
00:17:10,150 --> 00:17:12,780
你要和我聊聊你的想法吗
Are you gonna talk to me about whatever's on your mind?

193
00:17:15,150 --> 00:17:16,410
听着 这
Look, it was...

194
00:17:17,410 --> 00:17:18,740
我什么都没想
It was nothing.

195
00:17:18,830 --> 00:17:21,450
你刚才又在尖叫了
You were screaming. Again.

196
00:17:25,210 --> 00:17:27,210
我没事
I'm fine.

197
00:17:28,420 --> 00:17:31,090
我觉得我们对于 没事 的理解不太一样
I think we have different understandings of the word "Fine."

198
00:17:39,220 --> 00:17:41,350
我们已经追踪手和会好几个月了
We've been chasing the Hand for months.

199
00:17:43,890 --> 00:17:46,890
我们终于找到了一个或许可以帮助我们的人了
We finally get a lead on a guy who can supposedly help us...

200
00:17:47,770 --> 00:17:50,020
可等我们赶到那里 却只能眼睁睁看着他死了
and we get there just in time to watch him die.

201
00:17:50,110 --> 00:17:52,650
这不是你的错
It is not your fault.

202
00:17:54,320 --> 00:17:55,650
那个女人在我手下逃走了
I let that woman escape.

203
00:17:55,740 --> 00:17:58,530
你又不是故意让她逃走的
You didn't let anyone do anything.

204
00:17:58,620 --> 00:18:01,370
不管她是谁 我从没见过这么快的移动速度
Whoever she was, she moved faster than anyone I've ever seen.

205
00:18:02,030 --> 00:18:03,450
是的
Yeah.

206
00:18:05,120 --> 00:18:06,660
她的进攻速度也很快
She hit like it, too.

207
00:18:11,750 --> 00:18:14,090
一定是手合会的人 是吧
It had to be the Hand, right?

208
00:18:15,800 --> 00:18:16,970
我不确定
I don't know.

209
00:18:18,430 --> 00:18:21,300
手合会里还有许多我不知道的秘密勾当
There are a lot of things that the Hand kept from me.

210
00:18:23,810 --> 00:18:26,480
这些勾当可没有那么容易对付
They're not the kind of problem that's gonna go away easily,

211
00:18:26,560 --> 00:18:28,100
不过我们会弄明白的
but we can figure this out.

212
00:18:29,310 --> 00:18:30,310
一起弄明白
Together.

213
00:18:37,240 --> 00:18:39,070
这帮人想在纽约干什么
What do they want in New York?

214
00:19:04,430 --> 00:19:07,180
请把衣服都脱了 首饰也请取下
You'll need to disrobe. Jewelry and all.

215
00:19:40,760 --> 00:19:42,130
抱歉让你久等了
Sorry to keep you waiting.

216
00:19:44,430 --> 00:19:45,550
上一轮测试的
The results of the last

217
00:19:45,550 --> 00:19:47,600
结果已经和你说明白了 对吗
round of tests were explained to you, yes?

218
00:19:49,730 --> 00:19:51,480
测试结果很明确
They're rather conclusive, I'm afraid.

219
00:19:53,060 --> 00:19:55,480
我的意思是
And by that, of course, what I mean to say is...

220
00:19:55,560 --> 00:19:56,770
我要死了
I'm dying.

221
00:19:58,990 --> 00:20:01,570
我的红细胞数量骤减
My red blood cell count has dropped precipitously

222
00:20:01,650 --> 00:20:05,570
每个重要的器官也将近衰竭
and almost every one of my major organs is close to collapse.

223
00:20:07,120 --> 00:20:08,370
情况还是这样吗
Is that still the case?

224
00:20:11,500 --> 00:20:12,920
你能怎么治疗呢
What can you do to treat it?

225
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:15,580
老实说 这么急转直下的情况已回天乏术
To be honest, this kind of free fall is off the charts.

226
00:20:15,670 --> 00:20:17,000
说这个有什么用
That's not helpful.

227
00:20:17,590 --> 00:20:19,170
我问你的是还能做点什么
Or even what I asked.

228
00:20:19,800 --> 00:20:23,470
好吧 不幸的是 即便如您一般拥有十分强大的资源
Well, unfortunately, even for someone with your resources...

229
00:20:24,510 --> 00:20:26,180
我们也做不了什么了
there's not much we can do.

230
00:20:31,640 --> 00:20:32,640
呃
Um...

231
00:20:34,190 --> 00:20:35,900
我还剩多少时间
how much time do I have left?

232
00:20:36,940 --> 00:20:39,820
几个月 或者几个星期
Could be months. Could be weeks.

233
00:20:41,740 --> 00:20:44,070
做个检查能给出更准确的答案
I think this should give us more definitive answers.

234
00:20:44,610 --> 00:20:45,450
这边请
Please.

235
00:21:04,840 --> 00:21:05,930
开始吧
Let's begin.

236
00:21:22,940 --> 00:21:24,610
天呐 我擦
Jesus. Shit.

237
00:21:24,700 --> 00:21:26,160
琼斯小姐吗
Ms. Jones?

238
00:21:27,030 --> 00:21:29,280
我是米歇尔 雷蒙德
My name is Michelle Raymond.

239
00:21:29,370 --> 00:21:31,790
这是我的女儿 请帮帮我们
This is my daughter, Lexi. We need your help.

240
00:21:32,790 --> 00:21:33,620
我无能为力
I can't.

241
00:21:33,700 --> 00:21:36,080
抱歉 我们这么冒昧地来到你这
I'm sorry. We weren't sure if we were in the right place.

242
00:21:36,170 --> 00:21:38,630
我现在帮不了你们 以后也不行
Not today. Probably not tomorrow, either.

243
00:21:38,710 --> 00:21:40,590
- 算了吧 妈妈 - 我知道你的事迹
- Come on, Mom. - I read about what you did.

244
00:21:40,670 --> 00:21:41,710
她根本不在乎
She doesn't give a shit.

245
00:21:41,800 --> 00:21:44,590
- 我的丈夫不见了 - 她反正只是个行走的废柴
- My husband is missing. - She's a walking shit show anyway.

246
00:21:46,010 --> 00:21:47,680
- 你说什么 - 莱克茜 别这样
- Excuse me? - Lexi, please.

247
00:21:48,590 --> 00:21:51,430
我们的情况不太好 他已经一周没有消息了
We are not doing great. He has been gone a full week.

248
00:21:51,510 --> 00:21:53,390
- 你报警了吗 - 没有
- Did you call the cops? - No.

249
00:21:53,470 --> 00:21:56,480
- 为什么不呢 警察帮你可不收费 - 这不是钱的问题
- Why not? They're free. - Money is not an issue.

250
00:21:56,560 --> 00:22:00,690
事情有蹊跷 我敢肯定 约翰一直很有规律
Something is wrong and I know it. John's like clockwork.

251
00:22:00,770 --> 00:22:03,780
他是建筑师 每天早上8点去上班
He's an architect. He goes to work every morning at eight.

252
00:22:03,860 --> 00:22:05,570
傍晚6:30回家
He comes back home every night at 6:30.

253
00:22:05,650 --> 00:22:08,160
- 但是最近他 - 变得不一样 行踪隐秘
- But lately, he's... -He's been different? Secretive?

254
00:22:08,240 --> 00:22:10,450
- 然后还有点神经质吗 - 一点都不像他
- Maybe even a little nervous? - And it's not like him.

255
00:22:10,530 --> 00:22:13,240
那是因为他背着你偷情 好吗
Because he's cheating on you, okay?

256
00:22:13,330 --> 00:22:15,960
你别不好意思 这种事太多了
Nothing to be ashamed about. It happens all the time.

257
00:22:16,040 --> 00:22:18,040
- 你不了解他 - 我没必要了解他
- You don't know him like I do. - I don't need to.

258
00:22:18,120 --> 00:22:21,090
是你来找我 我也给了你我的专业看法
But you came to me and I'm giving you my professional opinion.

259
00:22:21,170 --> 00:22:22,790
你该去找离婚律师
You need a divorce lawyer.

260
00:22:24,800 --> 00:22:26,550
谢谢您的帮助 琼斯小姐
Thank you for your time, Ms. Jones.

261
00:22:27,970 --> 00:22:29,890
我真是谢谢你了
Yeah, thanks so much.

262
00:22:31,680 --> 00:22:34,100
等会
Hey.

263
00:22:36,890 --> 00:22:40,480
不管他现在怎样 我希望你们能找到他
Whatever he's doing... I hope you find him.

264
00:22:58,750 --> 00:23:00,870
你打错了
Wrong number.

265
00:23:00,960 --> 00:23:02,330
杰西卡 琼斯
Jessica Jones,

266
00:23:02,420 --> 00:23:05,420
你别自招麻烦 不要去找约翰 雷蒙德
do yourself a favor and don't look for John Raymond.

267
00:23:06,170 --> 00:23:07,920
喂
Hello?

268
00:24:09,740 --> 00:24:10,940
你好 陌生人
Hey, stranger.

269
00:24:13,820 --> 00:24:15,570
一起喝杯咖啡怎么样
Should we get that coffee?

270
00:24:35,340 --> 00:24:37,350
等你出现可真是没准头啊
Waiting on you was a heck of a gamble.

271
00:24:38,850 --> 00:24:40,810
据我所知 你可不擅长这个
For all I knew, you could've sucked at this.

272
00:24:40,890 --> 00:24:42,560
是吗
Yeah?

273
00:24:42,640 --> 00:24:44,730
- 嗯 - 希望你没白等
- Mm-hmm. - Well, I hope I was worth it.

274
00:24:45,400 --> 00:24:46,520
你很有潜力
You got potential.

275
00:24:46,610 --> 00:24:48,610
- 潜力 是吗 - 嗯哼
- "Potential"? Yeah? -Mm-hmm.

276
00:24:48,690 --> 00:24:50,320
嗯
Mm-hmm

277
00:24:55,110 --> 00:24:57,910
在监狱里有段很艰难的日子
There were some really rough days inside.

278
00:24:58,990 --> 00:25:02,000
是你写的信 让我撑了过来
But your letters... they got me through it.

279
00:25:02,080 --> 00:25:04,830
我都不记得我上回手写信是什么时候了
I can't remember the last time I handwrote a letter.

280
00:25:07,170 --> 00:25:09,840
- 有次里面有一首诗 - 天呐
- There was that poem that one time. - Oh, God.

281
00:25:09,920 --> 00:25:13,300
- 别这样 那首诗很不错 - 谢谢你
- No, it was a good one. - Thank you.

282
00:25:13,550 --> 00:25:16,640
{\pos(192.8,271.067)}- 我是说 像是尼奇 吉奥瓦尼的 - 嘘
- I mean, it was also Nikki Giovanni. -Shh!

283
00:25:13,550 --> 00:25:16,640
{\pos(194.3,285.467)}尼奇·吉奥瓦尼:上世纪60、70年代著名非裔美国诗人

284
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,000
尼奇·吉奥瓦尼 上世纪60、70年代著名非裔美国诗人

285
00:25:16,720 --> 00:25:19,890
- 不错的 - 我们可没有都跟你似的那么多陈词滥调
- Yeah. - We all can't be your corny ass.

286
00:25:19,970 --> 00:25:21,810
陈词滥调也比抄袭别人的好多了
Hey, I'd rather be corny than to plagiarize.

287
00:25:21,890 --> 00:25:23,060
痛
Ow!

288
00:25:23,140 --> 00:25:25,350
我在这些信里注意到一些
There was something else I noticed about your letters...

289
00:25:26,230 --> 00:25:27,480
你没说的事情
What you didn't say.

290
00:25:28,150 --> 00:25:30,730
- 卢克 - 听着 我知道这套路
- Luke... - Look, I know the drill.

291
00:25:30,820 --> 00:25:33,570
我被关进去了 你觉得有些事你不能告诉我
Man goes inside, you think there are things you can't tell him.

292
00:25:34,400 --> 00:25:38,370
但是不管在哈林区发生了什么 我要弄清楚
But whatever's going on in Harlem... I'm gonna find out.

293
00:25:39,280 --> 00:25:42,290
听着 我们就不能好好享受这点时光吗
Look, can't we just enjoy this part a little longer?

294
00:25:46,670 --> 00:25:48,000
我得知道
I need to know.

295
00:25:48,630 --> 00:25:50,590
哈林区经历了一些变化
Harlem's gone through changes.

296
00:25:52,250 --> 00:25:54,010
这是无法避免的
It was bound to happen.

297
00:25:54,090 --> 00:25:55,220
玛利亚在干嘛
What's Mariah doing?

298
00:25:55,300 --> 00:25:57,550
就跟你走之前一样
The same shit she was doing when you left.

299
00:25:58,640 --> 00:26:03,430
好吧 现在你要担心的只剩下你自己了
Look, right now, the only thing you need to worry about is you.

300
00:26:03,520 --> 00:26:05,350
如果你说的是找工作
Look, if you're talking about getting a job,

301
00:26:05,430 --> 00:26:07,600
我可全心全意想找呢
I have every intention of doing just that.

302
00:26:07,690 --> 00:26:08,900
做什么
Doing what?

303
00:26:09,610 --> 00:26:13,690
你成了哈林区的英雄 哪还能有什么自己的生活
How does being Harlem's hero allow you to live an actual life?

304
00:26:13,780 --> 00:26:15,320
我会有办法的
I'll find a way.

305
00:26:16,900 --> 00:26:18,240
现在
Right now, just...

306
00:26:18,950 --> 00:26:20,450
我只想帮助人们
I just wanna help people.

307
00:26:20,530 --> 00:26:22,120
我也想这么做
I wanna do that, too.

308
00:26:23,370 --> 00:26:27,290
你可以说我自私 但是我更希望你照顾好自己
But call me selfish... I wanna see you take care of yourself.

309
00:26:38,130 --> 00:26:39,430
谁啊
Hello?

310
00:26:47,680 --> 00:26:49,400
- 嗨 - 嗨
- Hey. - Hey.

311
00:26:49,480 --> 00:26:51,190
- 祝你好运 - 谢谢
- Good look. - Thanks.

312
00:26:53,060 --> 00:26:58,570
抱歉打搅了 但是很高兴看到你已经安顿好了
Sorry to interrupt. But I'm glad to see you're settling in.

313
00:27:00,030 --> 00:27:02,370
嘿 米丝蒂 很高兴见到你
Hey, Misty. It's good to see you.

314
00:27:02,450 --> 00:27:03,870
也很高兴见到你 卢克
Good to see you, too, Luke.

315
00:27:05,200 --> 00:27:06,700
你怎么找到我的
How did you know where to find me?

316
00:27:06,790 --> 00:27:09,290
开玩笑 你可是哈林区的英雄
Are you kidding? You're the hero of Harlem.

317
00:27:10,250 --> 00:27:11,540
想出去走走吗
Wanna come for a walk?

318
00:27:12,500 --> 00:27:15,590
- 其实我 - 不会占用你太长时间 我保证
- Actually, I was, uh - It won't take long, I promise.

319
00:27:31,230 --> 00:27:32,480
二号桌的菜好了
Number two in the window.

320
00:27:34,440 --> 00:27:36,110
上周发生的事挺有趣
Great story last week.

321
00:27:36,190 --> 00:27:38,360
关于那个学校董事会的丑闻
The, uh... thing with the school board scandal.

322
00:27:38,440 --> 00:27:42,410
谢谢 埃里森现在基本上让我自主工作
Thank you. Yeah, Ellison's pretty much given me free reign.

323
00:27:42,490 --> 00:27:45,280
感觉像是我注定要去
It feels like what I'm meant to be doing or...

324
00:27:45,370 --> 00:27:47,580
我知道这听起来说不通
I don't know if that makes any sense.

325
00:27:49,040 --> 00:27:50,330
是啊 当然
Yeah. Of course.

326
00:27:51,620 --> 00:27:53,460
看起来你在做你一直想做的事
It looks like you're doing what you always wanted to.

327
00:27:55,090 --> 00:27:57,670
是啊 从尼尔森和默多克律所到现在和
Yeah, it's been a transition from the Nelson and Murdock days,

328
00:27:57,750 --> 00:27:59,970
大律所的合伙 确实经历了一个过渡期
from the partnership but, uh...

329
00:28:00,720 --> 00:28:03,130
嗯 打无偿法律援助的案子我还是挺高兴的
No, the pro bono work does make me happy.

330
00:28:03,220 --> 00:28:05,220
- 真棒 真是太 - 要咖啡吗
- That's great. That's really-- - Coffee?

331
00:28:05,300 --> 00:28:07,060
- 好 谢谢 - 谢谢
- Yes, thank you. - Thanks.

332
00:28:13,480 --> 00:28:15,650
糖在左边 奶在右边
Sugar's on the left. Cream's here on the right.

333
00:28:15,730 --> 00:28:18,230
- 奶油在右边 谢谢 - 不客气
- Cream on the right. Thank you. - Yes. You're welcome.

334
00:28:21,610 --> 00:28:23,030
- 对不起 - 是啊
- Sorry, it got... - Yeah.

335
00:28:24,530 --> 00:28:26,660
你会希望你一直就自己保守着你的秘密吗
Do you wish you'd kept your secret to yourself?

336
00:28:27,700 --> 00:28:28,700
不
No.

337
00:28:30,040 --> 00:28:31,620
我需要你知道
I needed you to know.

338
00:28:32,790 --> 00:28:33,970
我不确定自己在期待什么
I don't know what I expected,

339
00:28:33,970 --> 00:28:35,830
但是我 我确定我不能再骗你了
but I... I know I couldn't lie to you anymore.

340
00:28:38,630 --> 00:28:40,170
谢谢 我很感激你这么说
Thanks. I appreciate that.

341
00:28:42,880 --> 00:28:44,090
你想念它吗
Do you miss it?

342
00:28:45,140 --> 00:28:46,180
战衣 面具
The suit? The mask?

343
00:28:47,510 --> 00:28:48,510
不
No.

344
00:28:49,970 --> 00:28:52,140
就好像我人生中的这一章已经谢幕了
It feels like a chapter of my life that's closed.

345
00:28:53,100 --> 00:28:54,900
我不后悔 你知道的 我只是
Now, I don't regret it. You know, I just...

346
00:28:54,980 --> 00:28:57,690
- 我后悔因此赶跑了很多人 - 不
- I regret that it drove some people away. - No, it...

347
00:28:57,770 --> 00:29:00,070
听着 你的秘密没有把我赶跑 我只是
Look, it didn't drive me away. I just...

348
00:29:01,440 --> 00:29:02,820
我觉得我们
You know, I felt like we

349
00:29:02,830 --> 00:29:05,530
应该先解决好自己的问题
should figure ourselves out first or something.

350
00:29:07,120 --> 00:29:08,120
我一直在尝试
I'm trying.

351
00:29:09,290 --> 00:29:10,290
嗯
Hmm.

352
00:29:13,870 --> 00:29:15,600
尽管我感觉所有的这些事
You know, as complicated

353
00:29:15,600 --> 00:29:18,540
都是那么的复杂 我只是
as I feel about all this stuff, I just...

354
00:29:20,210 --> 00:29:21,710
我觉得你应该知道
I feel like you should know.

355
00:29:23,300 --> 00:29:24,680
纽约警局现在干实事了
The NYPD is prevailing.

356
00:29:24,760 --> 00:29:28,260
我每天都报道他们的事儿 犯罪率也确实下降了
I report on it every day, and crime rate's down.

357
00:29:28,350 --> 00:29:29,410
我确实认为
I really think that

358
00:29:29,410 --> 00:29:32,060
夜魔侠让这个城市更安全了
Daredevil may have made the city a safer place.

359
00:29:35,020 --> 00:29:36,230
也许有他的功劳
He might have.

360
00:29:37,400 --> 00:29:39,360
但是现在 这个城市没有了他更好
But right now, the city's better off without him.

361
00:29:39,440 --> 00:29:40,520
嗯
Hmm.

362
00:29:41,860 --> 00:29:45,150
有马克 默多克在的纽约城更好
Well, it's better off with Matt Murdock.

363
00:29:48,160 --> 00:29:49,620
说到这事 默多克先生
Speaking of which, Mr. Murdock...

364
00:29:50,740 --> 00:29:52,290
我想问问你对今天
I would like to take your

365
00:29:52,290 --> 00:29:55,500
亚伦 詹姆斯一案判决的看法
statement on today's miraculous Aaron James verdict.

366
00:29:55,580 --> 00:29:57,170
放马过来吧
Hit me.

367
00:30:07,260 --> 00:30:08,140
嘿
Hey.

368
00:30:08,220 --> 00:30:09,640
- 不行 - 干嘛
- No. - What?

369
00:30:09,720 --> 00:30:10,830
你别再那么干了
We are not doing that thing

370
00:30:10,830 --> 00:30:12,560
随随便便到这来 就跟去你家一样
where you come in here like you live here.

371
00:30:12,640 --> 00:30:14,850
- 是你给我的钥匙 - 是你没经过我同意
- You gave me a key. - You took the spare key

372
00:30:14,930 --> 00:30:17,060
就给家里换锁的时候自己拿的备用钥匙
when you changed the locks without my permission.

373
00:30:17,140 --> 00:30:19,230
门坏了 我是在帮你的忙
Door was broken, and I was doing you a favor.

374
00:30:19,310 --> 00:30:21,980
- 你想干嘛 马尔科姆 - 就来喝个汽水
- What do you want, Malcolm? - Just came for soda.

375
00:30:22,070 --> 00:30:24,440
- 哦 我们现在在干嘛 - 我们现在啥事儿没干
- Ooh! So what are we doing? - We are doing nothing.

376
00:30:24,530 --> 00:30:26,530
你接了个案子 我看得出来
You took a case. I can tell.

377
00:30:26,610 --> 00:30:29,530
- 你脸上有那种兴奋 - 我没接什么案子
- You've got that glow about you. - I did not take a case...

378
00:30:29,620 --> 00:30:31,160
- 目前还没有 - 那是谁
- yet. - Who is that?

379
00:30:31,240 --> 00:30:33,790
- 别从我肩膀后面看 - 好吧
- Don't read over my shoulder. - Okay.

380
00:30:33,870 --> 00:30:35,450
是个建筑师 对吗
It's an architect, huh?

381
00:30:35,540 --> 00:30:37,710
- 又是一个偷情的 - 也许
- Another cheater? - Maybe.

382
00:30:37,790 --> 00:30:39,960
他妻子来我这 迫切地想找到他
His wife showed up desperate to find him.

383
00:30:40,040 --> 00:30:41,960
她说了一大堆我之前就听过的事
She said a bunch of stuff I've heard before.

384
00:30:42,040 --> 00:30:44,380
你知道 意思就是 他是个正人君子 他很反常
You know, "He's squeaky clean. This is unlike him."

385
00:30:45,090 --> 00:30:46,630
但是后来我接了通电话
But then I got a call.

386
00:30:46,720 --> 00:30:49,340
有人用声音干扰器告诉我不要接这个案子
Someone used a voice scrambler and told me not to take the case.

387
00:30:49,430 --> 00:30:51,550
我猜你就喜欢这种 是不是
Bet you loved that, didn't you?

388
00:30:52,350 --> 00:30:53,640
毕业于麻省理工学院
Graduated MIT.

389
00:30:53,720 --> 00:30:57,060
在迪拜设计了两座摩天楼 在曼哈顿也设计了四座楼
Designed two skyscrapers in Dubai and four in Manhattan.

390
00:30:57,140 --> 00:30:59,350
他确实是个正人君子 你认为她妻子说得没错
He is squeaky clean. You think she's right?

391
00:30:59,440 --> 00:31:01,940
也许 又或者他厌倦了当个好人
Maybe. Maybe he's tired of being the good guy.

392
00:31:02,020 --> 00:31:04,650
也许他酗酒 也许他跟哪个实习生搞上了
Maybe he's on a bender. Maybe he's knee-deep in some intern.

393
00:31:04,730 --> 00:31:06,190
- 恶心 - 非常恶心
- Gross. - Very.

394
00:31:06,280 --> 00:31:07,820
所以 你有什么线索
So, what are your leads?

395
00:31:08,450 --> 00:31:09,560
我根本没在找线索
I'm not looking for leads,

396
00:31:09,560 --> 00:31:11,320
马尔科姆 因为我还没接这个案子
Malcolm, because I haven't take the case.

397
00:31:11,410 --> 00:31:13,580
是啊 你试着追踪他的电话了吗
Yeah, right. Have you tried tracking the call yet?

398
00:31:13,660 --> 00:31:16,290
行不通 电话号码能重新路由
It doesn't work that way. You can reroute phone numbers.

399
00:31:16,370 --> 00:31:17,910
我是说 也许他没在号码上做手脚
I mean, maybe he didn't, though.

400
00:31:18,000 --> 00:31:20,960
也许他只是个想要让你别找他的人
Maybe he's just a regular guy trying to throw you off the scent.

401
00:31:21,790 --> 00:31:23,380
- 也许 - 也许他是个业余的
- Maybe - Maybe he's an amateur.

402
00:31:29,970 --> 00:31:33,260
你好 我刚刚接到一个被屏蔽号码的电话
Hi. I just got a call from a blocked number.

403
00:31:33,340 --> 00:31:35,810
我想知道你是否能告诉是从哪里打来的
I was wondering if you can tell me where it was coming from.

404
00:31:37,640 --> 00:31:39,600
你能帮帮我嘛
Is there anything that you can do?

405
00:31:39,690 --> 00:31:42,440
你知道的 我觉得电话应该是我祖父打来的 他年纪非常大了
You know, I think it's my grandfather and he's senile

406
00:31:42,520 --> 00:31:44,270
他可能在尝试找到我
and he might be trying to get a hold of me.

407
00:31:44,360 --> 00:31:46,150
事实上 我这里有一个失踪人员的报告
Actually, I have a missing person's report.

408
00:31:46,230 --> 00:31:47,770
我这里正有一个号码
I have the number right in front of me.

409
00:31:47,770 --> 00:31:49,070
如果你需要我可以读给你
I can read it to you if you want.

410
00:31:49,740 --> 00:31:52,610
真的吗 太感谢你了
Really? Thank you so much.

411
00:31:54,120 --> 00:31:56,120
这年头还有谁会用公用电话啊
Who the hell uses pay phones anymore?

412
00:31:56,830 --> 00:31:59,910
- 在哪里 - 第11街和第49街交叉路口
- Where? - 11th and 49th.

413
00:32:04,420 --> 00:32:05,920
好吧 我知道这个地方
Ugh, I know this place.

414
00:32:06,960 --> 00:32:10,380
如果你要找的那个人在那个街区做些见不得人的事 那他就在那儿
If your guy's doing shady shit on that block, that's where he is.

415
00:32:10,470 --> 00:32:11,590
我曾经磕过海洛因
I used to do heroin.

416
00:32:11,680 --> 00:32:12,520
我懂的不多
I don't know much, but I

417
00:32:12,520 --> 00:32:13,970
但我知道人们去哪里逃避现实
know where people go to get off the grid.

418
00:32:21,060 --> 00:32:23,600
- 这是否意味着你接这个案子了 - 我想把我的钥匙拿回来
- Does this mean you're taking the case? -I want my key back.

419
00:32:23,690 --> 00:32:25,440
离开的我公寓
And get out of my apartment!

420
00:32:26,150 --> 00:32:27,270
还在警队里吗
Still in the force?

421
00:32:28,190 --> 00:32:29,990
你的确是干掉了响尾蛇
Just 'cause you took down Diamondback,

422
00:32:29,990 --> 00:32:31,360
但并不意味着犯罪就消失了
doesn't mean crime went away.

423
00:32:31,450 --> 00:32:33,240
我们是干掉了响尾蛇
We took down Diamondback.

424
00:32:33,990 --> 00:32:35,910
而现在我准备去干掉玛利亚和暗影了
And now I'm ready to take down Mariah and Shades.

425
00:32:35,990 --> 00:32:38,580
我真希望事情可以这么简单
I wish it was that easy.

426
00:32:39,620 --> 00:32:41,580
我知道他们在搞事情
I know their hands are in something.

427
00:32:42,540 --> 00:32:44,880
或许你需要另外一个游离于法律之外的帮手
Maybe you need another assist from outside the law.

428
00:32:44,960 --> 00:32:48,420
- 一个刚从号子里出来的人 - 那是以前的事儿的
- From somebody fresh out of lockup? - That's behind me.

429
00:32:49,050 --> 00:32:52,300
我现在已经把自己的过去弄干净了 我没有什么可隐瞒的了
Now that I've cleared up my past, I've got nothing to hide.

430
00:32:52,380 --> 00:32:54,300
看 我的团队正在处理这件事
Look, my team is on it.

431
00:32:55,050 --> 00:32:58,050
但哈林区会需要你的帮助
But Harlem could use your help...

432
00:32:58,140 --> 00:32:59,770
在你不再和小你的护士缠绵的时候
once you're done spending nights with the nurse

433
00:32:59,850 --> 00:33:04,060
- 是谁把缎带绑在橡树上的（借用黄丝带民谣调侃他） - 你有团队了啊
- who tied the ribbon round the oak tree. - Your team, eh?

434
00:33:04,810 --> 00:33:07,730
在你离开之后 我被任命到一个管辖全市的特遣队
When you left, I got put on a city-wide task force.

435
00:33:08,650 --> 00:33:09,900
听起来是升职了
Sounds like a promotion.

436
00:33:10,820 --> 00:33:14,320
我只能说我的打击的范围可不限于哈林区了
All I can say is my beat isn't just Harlem anymore.

437
00:33:15,030 --> 00:33:17,620
从现在开始 不要再犯错 这里终归还是家
Now, make no mistake, this is still home.

438
00:33:18,410 --> 00:33:21,120
- 无论发生好事还是坏事 - 这里发生了什么
- The good and the bad. - What happened here?

439
00:33:21,200 --> 00:33:24,870
官方说法 一个25岁的男人被发现死在一辆停着的车里
Officially, 25-year-old male found deceased in a parked car.

440
00:33:25,540 --> 00:33:27,380
那非官方的说法呢
And unofficially?

441
00:33:28,670 --> 00:33:30,340
我觉得有些人在利用哈林区的年轻人
I think somebody's been using Harlem's youth

442
00:33:30,420 --> 00:33:33,920
去做那些所谓的深夜任务
for what can only be described as late-night duty.

443
00:33:34,010 --> 00:33:35,800
- 做信使吗 - 可能
- Couriers? - Maybe.

444
00:33:36,510 --> 00:33:38,010
可能还和玛利亚有关
Might even be related to Mariah.

445
00:33:39,390 --> 00:33:40,680
你觉得可能是别的什么吗
You think it's something else.

446
00:33:40,760 --> 00:33:45,350
过去几个月已经有七个类似案例了
Seven in the last few months. Always the same story.

447
00:33:45,440 --> 00:33:48,100
哈林区一个20岁上下的年轻人的把他的母亲从贫民窟搬到了
Harlem 20-something moves his mom out of the projects

448
00:33:48,190 --> 00:33:51,530
新罗谢尔（纽约富人区）一个很好的房子里
into a nice home in New Rochelle.

449
00:33:51,610 --> 00:33:52,780
还是用现金支付的
Down payment in cash.

450
00:33:53,860 --> 00:33:55,070
这些事之间有什么联系吗
What's the connection between them?

451
00:33:55,150 --> 00:33:57,160
你查他们的档案 找人查证 显示
Run their names, you talk to people...

452
00:33:57,240 --> 00:34:00,740
都和枪支毒品无关 仅仅是有了份新的工作 查不到记录
No guns, no drugs, just a new job, off the books.

453
00:34:00,830 --> 00:34:02,700
他们是做什么的 没人知道
Doing what? Nobody knows.

454
00:34:03,660 --> 00:34:04,750
嗯
Hmm.

455
00:34:06,210 --> 00:34:08,250
你做好听真正悲哀的部分了嘛
You ready for the real sad part?

456
00:34:09,170 --> 00:34:12,840
还记得坎迪斯吗 差点就要出庭指控玛利亚了
You remember Candace? This close to testifying against Mariah?

457
00:34:12,920 --> 00:34:14,550
谋杀案还没有破得那个
Murder still unsolved?

458
00:34:15,920 --> 00:34:18,010
她是这个死者的姐姐
That was his sister.

459
00:34:21,720 --> 00:34:23,260
现在这家就剩一个孩子了
Now there's only one.

460
00:34:23,350 --> 00:34:25,810
你应该听听他们母亲的哭声
You should've heard the way their mother cried.

461
00:34:29,520 --> 00:34:30,900
这事你能让我接手多少
How much can you let me in on this?

462
00:34:31,480 --> 00:34:32,940
我会找到幕后主使的
I'll find who's behind it.

463
00:34:33,980 --> 00:34:35,740
你确实可以做到这个
You could do that.

464
00:34:36,440 --> 00:34:41,030
但或者你可以给这个活下来的年轻人指引明路
Or you could help guide this young man in a different direction.

465
00:34:41,660 --> 00:34:43,030
就像老爹曾经做的
The way Pop used to.

466
00:34:45,750 --> 00:34:48,370
你听说过那个清理了克里斯普斯 阿塔克斯的人吗
You hear about that cat that cleaned up Crispus Attucks?

467
00:34:48,460 --> 00:34:49,920
就是他 兄弟
That's him, man.

468
00:34:52,710 --> 00:34:54,460
听说他被关在格鲁吉亚的某个地方
Heard he was locked up somewhere down in Georgia.

469
00:35:15,190 --> 00:35:17,780
保佑我 神父 我身负罪孽
Uh, bless me, Father, for I have sinned.

470
00:35:19,280 --> 00:35:24,910
我已经有 嗯 三天没有忏悔了
It's been... uh, three days since my last confession.

471
00:35:28,830 --> 00:35:32,540
我今天对某人说谎了 一个我爱的人
I lied to someone. Someone I love.

472
00:35:34,380 --> 00:35:36,670
她问我是否想念以前的生活
She asked me if I, uh, miss the life.

473
00:35:38,340 --> 00:35:41,760
我的另外一种生活
The other life that I led.

474
00:35:44,010 --> 00:35:46,390
我告诉她我不想念
And I told her I didn't.

475
00:35:46,970 --> 00:35:48,230
承认谎言的存在
Acknowledging a lie is

476
00:35:48,230 --> 00:35:50,850
往往是通往真理的最好选择 我的孩子
often the best path to finding the truth, son.

477
00:35:51,900 --> 00:35:53,730
这种谎言
A lie like this one...

478
00:35:54,900 --> 00:35:56,730
通常是表明了你自己的犹豫不决
is often a sign of indecision.

479
00:35:57,320 --> 00:36:01,490
表明了你的想法和灵魂并没有统一
A sign that your mind and your soul are not yet aligned.

480
00:36:02,450 --> 00:36:05,330
好吧 我已经非常努力去忽略我的灵魂了
Well, I'm trying very hard to ignore my soul.

481
00:36:05,990 --> 00:36:08,660
主看到的和人看到的不一样
"The Lord sees not as man sees.

482
00:36:08,750 --> 00:36:11,330
人总是看着外在
Man looks on the outward appearance,

483
00:36:11,330 --> 00:36:13,920
但是主 看到的是内心
but the Lord... looks on the heart."

484
00:36:14,920 --> 00:36:16,500
可以详细说说吗 神父
If you could elaborate, Father.

485
00:36:16,590 --> 00:36:19,510
忽略并不能改变任何东西 马修
Ignoring doesn't change anything, Matthew.

486
00:36:19,590 --> 00:36:21,130
上帝知道你的内心
God knows your heart.

487
00:36:21,880 --> 00:36:24,550
让主来帮助你
Let him in so he can help.

488
00:36:24,640 --> 00:36:27,760
- 哪怕那内心已经破损了吗 - 尤其是破损的
- Even if that heart is damaged? - Especially if it's damaged.

489
00:36:29,850 --> 00:36:31,850
马修 我希望和你坦诚地交流
Matthew, I want to talk frankly.

490
00:36:32,560 --> 00:36:35,730
- 请讲 - 你说到的另一个生活
- Please. - This other life you led...

491
00:36:37,770 --> 00:36:39,610
就是你的心之所在吗
is your heart still with it...

492
00:36:40,780 --> 00:36:44,200
还是说你的心更在于那个和你一起经历那个生活的人
or is your heart with the one who walked through it by your side?

493
00:36:46,030 --> 00:36:47,700
是艾丽卡 是的
Elektra. Yeah.

494
00:36:48,370 --> 00:36:49,660
我很想念她
I do miss her.

495
00:36:52,250 --> 00:36:55,290
但是我知道她从我身上发掘出的东西是错的
But I know that the things she brought out of me were wrong.

496
00:36:55,380 --> 00:36:57,170
从你告诉我和她有关的信息中看
From what you've told me about her,

497
00:36:57,250 --> 00:37:00,210
我想她会很高兴你现在过得很好
I think she'd be happy about how well you're doing.

498
00:37:00,300 --> 00:37:01,300
或许吧
Maybe.

499
00:37:02,220 --> 00:37:05,050
或者她会告诉我正抛弃那段生活
Or maybe she'd tell me I'm abandoning that life.

500
00:37:05,140 --> 00:37:07,050
还有对她的记忆
And with it, her memory.

501
00:37:07,140 --> 00:37:09,930
你并没有抛弃艾丽卡 你并不是这样的人
You're not abandoning Elektra. You don't have it in you.

502
00:37:10,770 --> 00:37:14,230
你现在的做法 我们称之为向前看
What you're doing, we call that moving on.

503
00:37:15,190 --> 00:37:18,360
炼狱是为死人准备的 马修 不是活人
Purgatory is a place for the dead, Matthew, not the living.

504
00:37:18,440 --> 00:37:21,070
放下一些人并没有什么问题
There's nothing wrong with letting people go.

505
00:37:21,990 --> 00:37:23,690
她会找到她的安宁的
She'll find her peace.

506
00:37:27,200 --> 00:37:29,620
你希望你也能找到你的安宁
I pray you find yours as well.

507
00:37:50,390 --> 00:37:52,270
你总是很喜欢这个地方
You always liked this spot.

508
00:37:55,560 --> 00:37:56,850
这个公园
It's a miracle...

509
00:37:58,150 --> 00:38:00,730
还存在着 这个城市还没有
the fact that this park even exists.

510
00:38:02,280 --> 00:38:06,780
把这儿拆了建高楼大厦 真是个奇迹
The fact that this city hasn't torn it down to put up high-rises.

511
00:38:10,410 --> 00:38:12,780
对这些人来说 要想象
Must be hard for these people to

512
00:38:12,790 --> 00:38:16,500
整个曼哈顿岛是一片森林的样子肯定很难
imagine the whole island of Manhattan as a forest.

513
00:38:19,630 --> 00:38:22,500
你知道 那些荷兰的殖民者
You know, the Dutch colonists...

514
00:38:24,130 --> 00:38:26,760
当初从原住民手上把曼哈顿买过来的时候
when they bought Manhattan from the natives,

515
00:38:26,840 --> 00:38:31,510
据说才花了24美刀
they're said to have acquired the whole thing for... $24.

516
00:38:34,720 --> 00:38:38,850
要我说 他们买贵了
Ask me, they overpaid.

517
00:38:41,860 --> 00:38:45,360
市长办公室的联系人 他准备好了
The contact at the mayor's office... he's ready.

518
00:38:46,070 --> 00:38:49,200
- 我们多久才能开始 - 三个月
- How soon can we begin? - Three months.

519
00:38:49,280 --> 00:38:51,370
然后我们就进入了最后阶段
Then we move to the final phase.

520
00:38:51,450 --> 00:38:53,620
那就行不通了 现在不行了
That won't work. Not anymore.

521
00:38:54,490 --> 00:38:57,580
- 我们要动作快一点 - 我们之前一致同意
- We need to move faster. - We all agreed.

522
00:38:57,660 --> 00:39:00,500
- 这个方案的 - 此一时彼一时
- This plan, it makes sense. - Made sense.

523
00:39:01,710 --> 00:39:04,420
为了安排这些 我们花了很大的代价
It took great efforts to arrange this.

524
00:39:05,050 --> 00:39:08,510
如果我们加快进度 恐怕会动静太大
If we speed the process, it will not be quiet.

525
00:39:09,380 --> 00:39:10,590
我知道
I'm aware.

526
00:39:14,310 --> 00:39:16,270
我会通知其他人的
I will inform the others.

527
00:39:16,350 --> 00:39:19,810
好 顺便帮我问候一下他们
Good. Send my regards when you do.

528
00:39:22,440 --> 00:39:26,690
然后喂完这些鸟 好吗
And, uh... finish feeding the birds, will you?

529
00:39:29,400 --> 00:39:31,110
它们今天很饿
They're starving today.

530
00:39:57,600 --> 00:39:59,140
你们知道在哪里能找到科尔吗
You guys know where I can find Cole?

531
00:39:59,890 --> 00:40:01,190
和你有什么关系
What's it to you?

532
00:40:07,360 --> 00:40:08,570
往上一楼
Uh, one floor up.

533
00:40:09,490 --> 00:40:10,490
谢谢
Thanks.

534
00:40:33,090 --> 00:40:36,640
我告诉过你们不要再放歌了
Man, I told y'all to stop playing!

535
00:40:38,350 --> 00:40:40,020
我来这里是为了表达我的敬意
I'm here to pay my respects.

536
00:40:42,890 --> 00:40:44,060
凯奇
Cage.

537
00:40:44,850 --> 00:40:46,650
我知道你是谁
I know who you are.

538
00:40:51,110 --> 00:40:53,700
- 你认识肖恩吗 - 不认识
- Did you know Sean? - No.

539
00:40:55,030 --> 00:40:56,570
但我认识你的姐姐坎迪斯
But I knew your sister Candace.

540
00:40:57,740 --> 00:40:59,870
我想我也是来替她表达敬意的
I guess I'm here to pay my respects for her, too.

541
00:40:59,950 --> 00:41:01,660
这个家庭确实倒霉 不是吗
This family's got some luck, huh?

542
00:41:03,620 --> 00:41:07,090
在这里 不好的事情往往会发生在好人身上
Around here, bad things have a tendency to happen to good people

543
00:41:09,000 --> 00:41:10,030
你觉得你弟弟的死
Do you think your brother's

544
00:41:10,030 --> 00:41:11,510
和她的死有关吗
death could somehow be related to hers?

545
00:41:11,590 --> 00:41:13,050
不 我不觉得
No. I don't think...

546
00:41:15,590 --> 00:41:19,100
不 发生在肖恩身上的事情 更像是一场意外
No, what happened to Sean was, um... was more like an accident.

547
00:41:20,180 --> 00:41:21,980
- 你确定吗 - 是的
- You sure about that? - Yeah.

548
00:41:25,230 --> 00:41:26,690
我听说他找到了一份新工作
I heard he got a new job.

549
00:41:27,270 --> 00:41:28,650
我不知道
I ain't know nothing about that.

550
00:41:29,480 --> 00:41:33,610
我是说 我们并非无话不谈 这是他的事
I mean, we didn't talk about everything. That was his business.

551
00:41:34,570 --> 00:41:35,570
当然
Of course.

552
00:41:37,370 --> 00:41:38,490
你呢
What about you?

553
00:41:39,200 --> 00:41:40,240
什么
What?

554
00:41:42,330 --> 00:41:44,000
情况似乎都还好
Things seem to be going okay.

555
00:41:45,920 --> 00:41:47,380
你有新的工作吗
Did you get a new gig?

556
00:41:49,250 --> 00:41:52,800
没有 我现在正在赋闲状态
No. I'm just in between stuff right now.

557
00:41:53,420 --> 00:41:55,340
你了解吗
I'm always on that hustle, though. You feel me?

558
00:41:55,430 --> 00:41:56,550
我知道
I do.

559
00:41:59,300 --> 00:42:02,470
听着 我可以帮你
Listen... I can help you.

560
00:42:03,060 --> 00:42:05,520
假如 如果你需要什么
Hypothetically speaking, if you ever need anything...

561
00:42:06,060 --> 00:42:07,350
我觉得你应该走了
I think you should go.

562
00:42:09,060 --> 00:42:12,000
问问这个街区的人我做了什么
Ask anybody on this block what I've done.

563
00:42:12,000 --> 00:42:13,860
或者我愿意做什么
Or what I'm willing to do.

564
00:42:15,200 --> 00:42:16,240
你可以相信我
You could trust me.

565
00:42:16,320 --> 00:42:17,340
这些都太晚了
It's too late for all of that.

566
00:42:17,340 --> 00:42:18,490
太晚了 是什么意思
What do you mean, "It's too late"?

567
00:42:18,570 --> 00:42:20,160
- 没什么 - 孩子 没有什么太晚
- Nothing. - Son, it's never too late--

568
00:42:20,240 --> 00:42:21,950
嘿 我不是你的儿子
Yo, man, I ain't your son!

569
00:42:22,660 --> 00:42:24,830
我告诉过你 我什么都不知道
I told you, I don't know a damn thing.

570
00:42:28,540 --> 00:42:31,380
不管你在做什么 你都会伤害你自己的
Whatever you're doing, you're gonna get yourself hurt.

571
00:42:33,340 --> 00:42:34,880
想想你的妈妈
Think about your mom.

572
00:42:36,760 --> 00:42:38,380
她经历了什么
What she's already been through.

573
00:42:48,140 --> 00:42:49,810
我觉得你应该走了
I think you should go.

574
00:42:52,570 --> 00:42:55,320
唯一能帮我的方法是让我也像你一样刀枪不入
The only way to help me is to make me bulletproof, too.

575
00:42:58,610 --> 00:43:00,120
你们这些英雄来得太晚了
It's too late for heroes.

576
00:43:01,910 --> 00:43:04,120
英雄是你说的 我可没这么说
Hero's your word. Not mine.

577
00:43:17,300 --> 00:43:20,430
- 我要我的钱 - 我听到了 我会去拿的
- I want my money. - I hear you. I'm gonna get it.

578
00:43:20,510 --> 00:43:22,550
你今天必须给我钱
You got till the end of the day,

579
00:43:22,640 --> 00:43:24,560
不然我会回来砸烂这地方
or I'm coming back here to bust some shit up!

580
00:43:46,910 --> 00:43:49,290
你好 约翰 雷蒙德 我是杰西卡 琼斯
Hey, John Raymond, it's Jessica Jones.

581
00:43:50,250 --> 00:43:53,080
我是来 回你电话的
I'm, uh... returning your call.

582
00:43:53,170 --> 00:43:55,380
你还记得你打了个电话想吓唬我来着吗
You remember the one where you tried to scare me?

583
00:44:00,430 --> 00:44:03,010
楼下的人说你在这里面
The guy downstairs said you were here.

584
00:44:03,760 --> 00:44:04,960
老兄 我不管你在搞什么
Dude, I don't care what

585
00:44:04,960 --> 00:44:07,140
奇怪的破事 但我们得谈一谈
weird shit you're into, but we gotta talk.

586
00:44:10,770 --> 00:44:13,020
好吧 这门锁得你自己花钱修了
All right, well, you're gonna pay for this.

587
00:44:51,140 --> 00:44:54,190
帮助刺激缓慢发展的欧元区经济
...and help stimulate a slow Eurozone economy...

588
00:45:01,950 --> 00:45:03,420
爆炸物和爆炸物示踪剂(为了观察爆炸物行为和性质而加入的指示剂)

589
00:45:03,950 --> 00:45:05,240
老天
Holy shit.

590
00:45:16,710 --> 00:45:17,540
谢谢
Thank you.

591
00:45:28,600 --> 00:45:31,220
按照你的要求 我们做了安排
We made arrangements, as you requested.

592
00:45:34,730 --> 00:45:36,450
你确定吗
Are you certain about this?

593
00:45:36,450 --> 00:45:38,940
现在还有时间可以考虑清楚的
There's still time to think it through.

594
00:45:40,230 --> 00:45:41,280
你可以走了
You can go.

595
00:45:57,000 --> 00:46:00,000
- 世界上最棒的城市 - 是的
- Greatest city in the world. - Yeah.

596
00:46:00,800 --> 00:46:02,300
纽约人喜欢这么说
New Yorkers like saying that.

597
00:46:04,380 --> 00:46:07,180
不过 在这段时间之后 我
Still, after all this time, I...

598
00:46:09,010 --> 00:46:10,430
我不知道我是怎么想的了
I don't know how I feel about it.

599
00:46:11,260 --> 00:46:14,810
这就是它的美妙之处 它可以是任何你需要的东西
That's the beauty of it. It can be whatever you need it to be.

600
00:46:16,850 --> 00:46:18,190
你需要它成为什么
What do you need it to be?

601
00:46:19,770 --> 00:46:20,770
家
Home.

602
00:47:19,830 --> 00:47:22,750
中央银行周三利率维持不变
...Central Bank on Wednesday kept interest rates unchanged,

603
00:47:22,840 --> 00:47:25,630
顶着加入其他主要重要银行的压力
resisting pressure to join other major central banks...

604
00:47:32,890 --> 00:47:33,890
谢谢
Thanks.

605
00:48:26,110 --> 00:48:27,530
这只是一个城市
It's just a city.

606
00:48:29,190 --> 00:48:32,360
你会习惯看着他们倒下的
You'll get used to watching them fall.

607
00:48:57,640 --> 00:48:59,770
我们得马上下去 爬楼梯
We gotta get down right away. Take the stairs!

608
00:48:59,850 --> 00:49:01,310
快往楼梯下跑
Get down the stairs!

609
00:49:16,950 --> 00:49:19,910
您拨打的电话正忙 请核对后再拨打
...you have dialed. Please check the number and dial again.

